lines+=['', 'R69 VAL1280 contains 1,033 unique media frames in the same five recordings used by prior target VAL development; historical full-VAL exposure was already disclosed. TRAIN1024 contains 1,024 unique media frames from four additional official recordings/place-name families selected in R69. It is not a source-training stage, and target labels do not enter evidence construction. Nominal recording/place-family separation does not certify a global geographical or absolute wall-clock holdout. Both cohorts already received R69 evaluation, so this is fixed-configuration expanded evaluation, not blind independent testing. FINAL files are neither decoded nor inferred nor scored, and no FINAL exclusion manifests are newly read.','', 'The same first-lexicon-noun/all-content-fallback source token readout from R69 remains unchanged; this is not a fresh reproduction of all official annotated-span protocols. Literal CLIP subject parsing may also retain wrong roles or lose attributes. Neither is repaired by test labels in this round. Long CLIP phrases retain R70 token coverage through at-most-75-token chunks plus special tokens and normalized weighted feature averaging; composition across chunks is not preserved. Tokenizer length warnings do not mean an oversized sequence is passed to the model.','', '## Input equivalence, audits and costs','', 'The field-minimized projection preparer omits B’s unused RGB patches and complex reliability calculations. All 336 cached DEV direct readouts are bit-exact to R70, with raw group/projection reconstruction on a preselected subset before expanded inference. Four engineering inputs cover VAL/TRAIN × Drone/Quad. Main CPU preparation and the single CLIP GPU reader run as a streaming pipeline; every consumed preparation/case file is matched to the final input seal before CLIP evidence is sealed. This changes scheduling, not evidence math.','',f"Main encoding uses {clip['image_crops']:,} crops across 2,304 inputs, {prepare['groups']:,} candidate groups and {prepare['projected_groups']:,} projected groups. Preparation {prepare['seconds']:.2f}s; CLIP encoding {clip['seconds']:.2f}s; max allocated CLIP GPU memory {clip['peak_GPU_bytes']/2**30:.3f} GiB. No new source forward, optimizer step, adapter fit, external detector, Qwen, SAM or DINO output is used. Timings include relevant cache/I/O and are marginal to existing source captures; they are not full deployment latency. CPU preparation overlaps encoding, so do not sum those times as wall-clock time.", '',f"All 2,640 observations × five arms are sealed before saved candidate-IoU lookup. CPU audit verifies every source A256/readout, original R69/R70 baseline, strict valid-group permutation and unknown pattern. Independent float64 probability arithmetic is bounded by the softmax Jacobian roundoff bound while native float32 replay is exact; maximum independent error {aud['max_float64_independent_probability_error']:.3g}. Expanded media hashes match the original R69 selected inputs. GPU audit reconstructs raw point-support groups and camera projections for {gpu['n']} fixed scene-stratified observations across {gpu['scene_clusters']} clusters, reencodes {gpu['CLIP_reencoded_crops']} crops and checks literal text embeddings; maximum image feature error {gpu['max_image_feature_error']:.3g}. Independent scalar audit verifies all {scalar['task_values']:,} saved-IoU task values and {scalar['ordered_negatives']:,} ordered negative comparisons. A separate audit checks every derived method/frame/scene/decision table.", '', 'All 2,304 expanded input records omit explicit distortion coefficients; the declared zero-distortion assumption is inherited unchanged from R70, not estimated from task labels. Camera projections and rectangular crops remain imperfect instance correspondence: background and neighboring instances may enter a crop; no true RGB instance mask or dense depth is introduced. The fixed CLIP model supplies external pretrained semantic knowledge. Direct-use improvement therefore supports useful visual evidence, not an innovation or parameter-TTA increment. With few scene clusters and prior development exposure, frame/scene tables describe variability; no expression-independent significance or certified new-domain generalization is asserted.','', '## Decision and next boundary','', outcome, '', 'Random RGB training and the R70 score-distillation adapter remain paused. No new update loss, adapter step budget, trainable layer, source retraining or FINAL evaluation is queued. If parameter adaptation is pursued later, its zero-step state must preserve the strong direct reader and its supervision must contribute information beyond copying that reader. It must beat a same-information direct-use control; this round does not test or establish that mechanism.','', 'Public artifacts include original owned code, frozen configuration, input/dependency/prediction hashes, anonymous per-observation and scene/frame scalars, all negative comparisons and audit receipts. Raw media, descriptions, camera coordinates, sample/scene identities, features, actual weights, secrets and third-party snapshots are excluded. Full reproduction requires the official data and exact source checkpoint; this package is not a standalone dataset/model distribution.']
